SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia's parliament lifts state of emergency early","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-02-16","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/02/16/us-ethiopia-conflict","claim":"Ethiopia's parliament voted to end the six-month state of emergency immediately, and Reuters reported diplomats were cautiously optimistic that progress toward peace was being made.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting on a dated parliamentary decision with direct conflict context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to de-escalation and restoration of normal governance.","ruler_attribution":"This reflects Abiy Ahmed's government moving from emergency powers toward regular law enforcement and parliamentary approval.","contrary_evidence":["The war was still ongoing in northern Ethiopia.","Ending emergency rule did not resolve humanitarian access or accountability."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"AU Commission Welcomes Key Confidence-Building Measures Towards the Peaceful Resolution of The Conflict in Ethiopia","publisher":"African Union","publication_date":"2022-06-16","url":"https://au.int/sw/node/41921","claim":"The AU Chairperson said confidence-building measures already undertaken included lifting the national state of emergency, release of detainees and prisoners of war, setting up the National Dialogue Commission, a humanitarian truce and ceasefire, and the withdrawal of TPLF from Afar.","locator":"body paragraph summarizing measures","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official AU statement naming multiple dated measures and directly tying them to peace efforts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and strong for the mid-year peace trajectory.","ruler_attribution":"These are ruler-linked state measures under Abiy Ahmed's government, though some items are mediated or bilateral rather than unilateral.","contrary_evidence":["The AU statement is supportive and does not test implementation durability.","It does not by itself prove civilian protection or lawful conduct on the ground."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Welcoming Ethiopian Government’s Declaration of Indefinite Humanitarian Truce, Secretary-General Urges All Parties to Take Steps towards Lasting Ceasefire","publisher":"United Nations","publication_date":"2022-03-25","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sgsm21207.doc.htm","claim":"The Secretary-General welcomed Ethiopia's indefinite humanitarian truce and called for restoration of public services in Tigray, including banking, electricity, and telecommunications, and for a long-term ceasefire.","locator":"opening statement paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN press statement directly records the declaration and the requested follow-through.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and central to the year's peace/de-escalation record.","ruler_attribution":"This is a government decision under Abiy Ahmed that moved the conflict toward de-escalation, though implementation remained uncertain.","contrary_evidence":["The statement assumes compliance by all parties and does not prove it.","Fighting and access restrictions later continued in parts of the country."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"AUC Chairperson Welcomes the Declaration of An Indefinite Humanitarian Truce by The Ethiopian Government in Tigray Region","publisher":"African Union","publication_date":"2022-03-25","url":"https://au.int/ar/node/41624","claim":"The AU Chairperson welcomed Ethiopia's indefinite humanitarian truce, welcomed Tigray's cessation of hostilities announcement, and called for a negotiated permanent comprehensive ceasefire and dialogue.","locator":"statement body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official AU reaction confirms the truce and frames it as part of a negotiated peace track.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and useful corroboration of the truce moment from a second official source.","ruler_attribution":"This supports attribution to Abiy Ahmed's government because the truce was a federal decision, but the statement is not a direct performance audit.","contrary_evidence":["The AU was urging further steps, implying the truce was not yet sufficient.","It does not address battlefield conduct or accountability."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia: Government, Tigrayan forces agree to end two-year war","publisher":"Al Jazeera reporting Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/news/2022/11/2/ethiopias-warring-sides-agree-cessation-of-hostilities-au","claim":"The parties agreed to a permanent cessation of hostilities, orderly disarmament, restoration of services, and humanitarian access; Abiy Ahmed hailed the breakthrough and committed to work toward implementation.","locator":"article body and quoted statement","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting summarized with concrete agreement terms and a direct Abiy quotation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and the key late-year peace pivot.","ruler_attribution":"The agreement was signed by representatives of Abiy Ahmed's government, making it strong ruler-attributed peace-process evidence.","contrary_evidence":["The report also notes the war had killed thousands and displaced millions.","It does not show full implementation or durable compliance."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Secretary-General Welcomes Signing of Peace Agreement between Ethiopia Government, Tigray People's Liberation Front","publisher":"United Nations","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sgsm21566.doc.htm","claim":"The Secretary-General called the signed agreement a critical first step toward ending the conflict and urged implementation, humanitarian access, restored public services, and continued negotiations on outstanding issues.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN statement directly summarizes the deal and the expected next steps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and central to post-agreement assessment.","ruler_attribution":"This is a direct response to the federal government's signing of the agreement under Abiy Ahmed's premiership.","contrary_evidence":["It is an endorsement, not verification of compliance.","The UN also signals unresolved issues remained."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement attributable to the Spokesperson for the Secretary-General - on Ethiopia","publisher":"United Nations","publication_date":"2022-11-13","url":"https://www.un.org/sg/en/content/sg/statements/2022-11-13/statement-attributable-the-spokesperson-for-the-secretary-general-ethiopia","claim":"The Secretary-General welcomed an implementation agreement between senior commanders of the Ethiopian army and the Tigrayan People’s Liberation Front and urged immediate concrete improvements for civilians through humanitarian access and restored services.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN statement directly ties the November agreement to implementation modalities and civilian relief.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and highly relevant to whether the peace deal was operationalized.","ruler_attribution":"This is ruler-attributed through the federal army command and the government-led implementation process.","contrary_evidence":["The statement implies implementation still needed to be translated into practice.","It does not prove that access or services were actually restored everywhere."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"“We Will Erase You from This Land”: Crimes Against Humanity and Ethnic Cleansing in Ethiopia’s Western Tigray Zone","publisher":"Human Rights Watch and Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-04-06","url":"https://www.hrw.org/report/2022/04/06/we-will-erase-you-land/crimes-against-humanity-and-ethnic-cleansing-ethiopias","claim":"The report says Amhara regional security forces and civilian authorities in Western Tigray committed widespread abuses against Tigrayans with the acquiescence and possible participation of Ethiopian federal forces, including unlawful killings, sexual violence, detention, pillage, forcible transfer, and denial of humanitarian assistance.","locator":"opening summary and findings sections","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed rights report based on extensive interviews and field research; strong for atrocity and responsibility allegations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"In-period evidence of ongoing wartime conduct and civilian harm in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The allegation reaches the federal government through acquiescence and possible participation, making it relevant to Abiy Ahmed's command environment.","contrary_evidence":["The report is region-specific, not a full national audit.","It alleges possible federal participation in some conduct rather than proving every act by direct Abiy order."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.5","2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Secretary-General's remarks to the Press on Ethiopia [as delivered]","publisher":"United Nations","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://www.un.org/sg/en/content/sg/press-events/2022-10-17/secretary-generals-remarks-the-press-ethiopia-delivered","claim":"The Secretary-General said the situation in Ethiopia was spiraling out of control, that there was no military solution, that Eritrean forces were inside Ethiopia, and that civilians were paying a horrific price from indiscriminate attacks and sexual violence.","locator":"speech text","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"High-level UN statement summarizing the late-2022 crisis conditions and external military dimension.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and important contrary evidence against a fully peaceful posture.","ruler_attribution":"This is adverse evidence for Abiy Ahmed's security conduct because it concerns the federal conflict under his premiership and the presence of Eritrean forces in Ethiopia.","contrary_evidence":["It is a UN characterization, not a legal finding.","It addresses wartime conditions rather than a separate interstate war initiated by Ethiopia."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.5","2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"WFP accelerates humanitarian operations in Northern Ethiopia","publisher":"World Food Programme","publication_date":"2022-11-25","url":"https://www.wfp.org/news/wfp-accelerates-humanitarian-operations-northern-ethiopia","claim":"WFP said it had delivered over 2,400 metric tons of food, medical, nutrition, and other lifesaving supplies to Tigray after the peace agreement and reopening of all four road corridors, though deliveries still fell short of needs.","locator":"opening paragraphs and bullet points","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Operational humanitarian monitoring from the UN system with concrete logistics figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and useful for end-of-year implementation effects.","ruler_attribution":"This is indirect but strong evidence that the federal government's post-agreement posture allowed materially improved humanitarian access.","contrary_evidence":["The source says deliveries still did not match needs.","It does not show full normalization or accountability."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNHCR ramps up assistance to refugees, displaced families in northern Ethiopia as peace returns","publisher":"UNHCR","publication_date":"2022-12-09","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/us/news/briefing-notes/unhcr-ramps-assistance-refugees-displaced-families-northern-ethiopia-peace","claim":"UNHCR said the peace agreement brought a major change in humanitarian access, with 61 trucks sent into Tigray, reopened field locations, and the assisted relocation of more than 7,000 Eritrean refugees.","locator":"briefing-note body","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNHCR field update with concrete operational indicators and named government counterpart service.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and useful for measuring post-agreement end-state change.","ruler_attribution":"This is relevant to Abiy Ahmed because it shows federal authorities enabled or permitted improved access after the peace agreement.","contrary_evidence":["The update still describes a conflict-affected relief response.","It does not establish full security normalization."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"OHCHR-EHRC joint advisory note on Transitional Justice","publisher":"United Nations in Ethiopia","publication_date":"2022-12-19","url":"https://ethiopia.un.org/en/212601-ohchr-ehrc-joint-advisory-note-transitional-justice","claim":"The note welcomed the 2 November 2022 peace agreement and quoted Article 10(3), which requires Ethiopia to implement a comprehensive national transitional justice policy aimed at accountability, truth, redress, reconciliation, and healing.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Joint UN/EHRC note directly cites the peace agreement and the transitional-justice obligation it creates.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to accountability after conflict.","ruler_attribution":"This is ruler-attributed because it describes commitments of the federal government under Abiy Ahmed's premiership.","contrary_evidence":["The note is prospective and consultative, not proof of implementation.","It reflects an accountability requirement that still had to be delivered."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The federal government approves the resumption of UNHAS flights to Tigray and humanitarian operations in northern Ethiopia","publisher":"United Nations in Ethiopia","publication_date":"2022-11-24","url":"https://ethiopia.un.org/en/164315-update-humanitarian-operations-northern-ethiopia","claim":"UN humanitarian partners reported that the federal government approved the resumption of UNHAS flights to Tigray and that convoys and food distributions had restarted after prior gaps, while access and supplies still remained constrained.","locator":"status-update paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Operational UN update with concrete references to federal approval and resumed access.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and useful for implementation after the peace pivot.","ruler_attribution":"This reflects government permissions under Abiy Ahmed's premiership, not a separate international actor decision.","contrary_evidence":["The update says the situation remained constrained.","It does not show full service restoration across the region."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"የኢትዮጵያ ፌደራል ፖሊስ የፌደራል ተቋማትን ለመጠበቅ መቀሌ ገባ","publisher":"Ethiopian News Agency (Amharic)","publication_date":"2022-12 (Ethiopian calendar Tahsas 20, 2015)","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/amh/w/am_199529","claim":"The article reports that, following the Pretoria peace agreement, Ethiopian federal police entered Mekelle to protect federal institutions and that federal services such as airports, electricity, telecommunications, and banking were expected to be protected.","locator":"lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Ethiopian state outlet in Amharic, but the exact Gregorian publication date is only indirectly recoverable from the Ethiopian calendar line in the snippet.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Late 2022 implementation context, though exact date conversion is approximate.","ruler_attribution":"This is ruler-linked implementation evidence under Abiy Ahmed because it describes federal deployment after the peace deal.","contrary_evidence":["The item is a state outlet report rather than independent verification.","It describes an implementation step, not full nationwide normalization."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents across these buckets:
- UN Secretary-General statements and press releases on Ethiopia
- AU Commission and AU mediation statements
- Reuters reports mirrored by Euronews and Al Jazeera
- HRW and Amnesty conflict/atrocity reporting
- WFP, UNHCR, UNICEF, UNAIDS, and UNDSS operational updates
- ENA English, Amharic, and Tigrinya material
- A few later retrospectives and summaries for implementation context

I rejected:
- Duplicate Reuters mirrors that repeated the same fact without adding a materially distinct claim.
- Out-of-period retrospectives from 2023-2026 when they only restated the same 2022 event.
- Broad commentary or explainer pieces that did not add Ethiopia-specific 2022 detail.
- Generic humanitarian background pages that were less useful than the direct UN operational updates kept above.
- Non-2B material on nuclear risk, corruption, or domestic liberties that belonged to other chapters.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no direct public source showing Abiy Ahmed personally making a 2022 external-war choice against a neighboring state. The local prior's zero internationalized-conflict figures matter here, and the dossier remains a limited-exposure 2B case rather than a classic interstate-war case.
- I did not find a public source proving direct Abiy command over Eritrean troop movements or a formal government acknowledgment of every allied atrocity in 2022.
- The weakest area is exact internal decision-making: public evidence shows the peace track and civilian harm, but not his private deliberations or command chain details.
- If you want to tighten the attribution and implementation side further, the next useful search would be archived Ethiopian-government or ENA Amharic/Tigrinya items from November-December 2022 on the Pretoria implementation steps, especially any statements on disarmament, federal force redeployment, and service restoration.
